Package: RegionSetDE
Type: Package
Title: Differential analysis of chromatin signal over user-defined genomic region sets, without peak calling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Sebastian", "Gregoricchio",
      email = "s.gregoricchio@nki.nl",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9209-5403")
    )
  )
Description:
  Differential analysis of chromatin profiling data over genomic
  regions supplied by the user, with no peak calling step. Regions are
  grouped into named sets of arbitrary width and size, such as promoter
  classes, enhancer catalogues or chromatin states, and are counted per
  region or per tile. Normalisation factors can be estimated from
  background bins or supplied externally, for instance from spike-in or
  greenlist approaches. A single model fit supports testing at two levels:
  individual regions, and whole region sets, including direct contrasts
  between two sets to ask whether a condition effect differs across
  classes of regions.
